hed  to the hospital said to be in relatively  good condition she was trapped for about  132 hours search crews had used sniffer  dogs and drones to find her  26 people were killed when the rear of  the building suddenly caved in on friday  at least nine people have been arrested  including the building's owner four  faced charges over liability suspected  of ignoring building codes  a young baseball fan had another  incredible moment last night to cap off  an unforgettable week nine-year-old  derek rodriguez met his baseball idol  new york yankee superstar aaron judge he  got the chance because of this this  beautiful moment when a blue jays fan  caught one of judge's home run balls and  handed it right over to the boy  rodriguez says he not only got to meet  his hero he also made a new best friend  next a bank settles with an indigenous  man and his granddaughter wrongly  accused and arrested in vancouver  an indigenous man and his granddaughter  who were arrested and handcuffed by  vancouver police after a bank accused  them of fraud have now reached a  settlement of their human rights  complaint against the bank of montreal  maxwell johnson an artist from the  heltzik nation was simply trying to add  his granddaughter's account to his own  bank employees not only refused they  called 9-1-1  now after two and a half years johnson  is reflecting on what he calls a long  hard journey  part of our culture is to forgive we  don't hold on to anything  maxwell johnson never wanted to be the  center of this story yet today he came  back to the same spot on a vancouver  street in front of a [ __ ] bank which  wrongly accused him and his  granddaughter of fraud his human rights  complaint against the bank finally  settled i'm just glad to be able to  stand up for myself and for my my kids  and grandkids and  other people that are afraid to come  forward to  stand their ground it was here two and a  half years ago that he and his then 12  year old granddaughter were arrested and  handcuffed all he tried to do was open a  bank account using their indigenous  status cards as id  the bank refused suspected fraud and  called the police  there was no evidence of fraud no  charges were laid and the bank has since  apologized  in april an independent review found the  two officers acted without reasonable  and probable grounds they were suspended  for several days it took  a lot of trust away from my  granddaughter my son and myself it's  been really hard  i suffer from a mental illness called  panic disorder  and i had to overcome the fear of uh  talking in public again  johnson lives here in the great bear  rainforest on bc's central coast a  member of the heltzik first nation he's  an artist and a cultural leader in his  community his work adorns the front of  the big house  his financial settlement with [ __ ] hasn't  been disclosed but for johnson this is  about so much more than money our people  have been on the coast for over 14 000  years  that's longer than the pyramids have  been up  so i just want people to educate  themselves more about first nations  issues and our culture  in the spirit of forgiveness he's  created this piece of art and gifted it  to the bank on the bottom it's got the  [ __ ] logo on there just  so is that we're working together to  get past this and  be on good terms it's good medicine  the officers who made the arrests have  been invited to an apology ceremony in  bella bella  they have yet to accept  johnson did one more thing today he  closed his bank account with [ __ ] if you  went through something i did you'd want  to change banks too  it is the end of a chapter he says but  not of the healing  late today [ __ ] put out a statement  saying it's pleased a settlement has  been reached and that it's an important  step in reconciliation  that is global national for this  thursday i'm donna friesen today was red  dress day in canada to remember the  countless indigenous women and girls  lost to racism and violence  we leave you tonight with some of the  gatherings across the country according  to the national inquiries final report  in 2019 indigenous women and girls were  12 times more likely to be murdered or  go missing in canada than any other  demographic  thanks for watching jeff sample will be  at the anchor desk tomorrow and i'll see  you on saturday for the new reality  bye
 

